2026-09-27T10:19:21.8395057Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8395432Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8395664Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8395944Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8396841Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8397238Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8397427Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8397894Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8398206Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8398457Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8399121Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8399823Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8401019Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8401996Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8402189Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8402947Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8403872Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8404358Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8404867Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8405609Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8405776Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8406410Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8406612Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8408929Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8411434Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8411839Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8412705Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8414111Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8415249Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8416559Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8483023Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8484168Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8484409Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8484911Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8485238Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8487353Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8489502Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8490674Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8492266Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:21.8492552Z 
